\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Taken together, this looks less like a \'93bad leader\'94 profile and more like a 
\f1\b high-drive, strategically minded leader who may become quite forceful under pressure, with unusually strong humility and reasonably strong empathy acting as important safeguards
\f0\b0 .\
One important caveat: without knowing the exact questionnaire, its scoring method, norms, reliability, and what each score means relative to its reference population, I would 
\f1\b not treat any individual number as a diagnosis or definitive personality trait
\f0\b0 . In particular, a high psychopathy or Machiavellianism score on a workplace questionnaire does not mean you have a clinical disorder. The most useful interpretation is to look at the 
\f2\i pattern
\f0\i0  and the situations in which those tendencies show up.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

