\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 6. Questions to ask yourself before applying any advice\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 This is important because leadership advice can easily become another tool for over-optimization.\
Before implementing a suggestion, ask:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \'93What problem am I actually trying to solve?\'94
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 Don't fix a trait simply because a questionnaire says it is elevated.\

\f1\b \'93Is this improving my leadership, or merely making me more comfortable?\'94
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b \'93What happens to people who have less power than I do?\'94
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 A strategy that works for an executive can be harmful when applied to junior employees.\

\f1\b \'93Would I make the same decision if my authority were not at stake?\'94
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b \'93Am I optimizing for the next result, or also for trust six months from now?\'94
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b \'93What evidence would tell me that my interpretation is wrong?\'94
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b \'93Who benefits from this decision, and who bears the cost?\'94
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b \'93Am I calling something \'91strategic\'92 because it is genuinely strategic, or because I want permission to avoid a difficult conversation?\'94
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b \'93Would I be comfortable explaining this decision openly to the people affected by it?\'94
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b \'93What would a highly ethical version of this strategy look like?\'94
\f0\b0 \
That last question is particularly well matched to your profile: 
\f1\b don't discard your strategic ability\'97ethicalize it.
\f0\b0 \
